WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.383 --> 00:00:04.000
Unit twelve. Nutrition Across Life!

2
00:00:04.941 --> 00:00:09.234
Hello, everyone! I'm Doctor Sokha, your school doctor.

3
00:00:09.284 --> 00:00:12.425
Hi, Doctor Sokha! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:12.475 --> 00:00:16.579
Today we learn about Nutrition Across Life. Let's go!

5
00:00:17.685 --> 00:00:21.618
Lifespan. Say it with me. Lifespan!

6
00:00:25.145 --> 00:00:29.212
Infancy. Say it with me. Infancy!

7
00:00:32.674 --> 00:00:37.074
Adolescence. Say it with me. Adolescence!

8
00:00:40.559 --> 00:00:44.776
Pregnancy. Say it with me. Pregnancy!

9
00:00:48.298 --> 00:00:52.598
Older adults. Say it with me. Older adults!

10
00:00:56.067 --> 00:00:59.884
Calcium. Say it with me. Calcium!

11
00:01:03.406 --> 00:01:07.406
Protein. Say it with me. Protein!

12
00:01:10.910 --> 00:01:15.026
Needs. Say it with me. Needs!

13
00:01:18.550 --> 00:01:30.598
Nutrition needs change across the lifespan. Infancy and adolescence need nutrients for growth, pregnancy needs extra folate and iron, and older adults need calcium and protein.

14
00:01:30.648 --> 00:01:34.051
Now I understand. Thank you, Doctor Sokha!

15
00:01:34.887 --> 00:01:40.244
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:40.294 --> 00:01:41.563
Adolescence!

17
00:01:42.639 --> 00:01:47.896
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:47.946 --> 00:01:49.096
Protein!

19
00:01:50.105 --> 00:01:56.172
Did you know? Older adults often need more protein to help keep their muscles strong!

20
00:01:56.222 --> 00:01:58.641
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:01:59.906 --> 00:02:08.460
Think and answer. How do nutrition needs change as people age?

22
00:02:08.510 --> 00:02:09.660
Great answer!

23
00:02:10.746 --> 00:02:16.155
Great job today! Stay healthy, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
00:02:16.205 --> 00:02:19.068
Goodbye, everyone! Stay healthy!

